
import streamlit as st
import gettext


localizator = gettext.translation('messages', localedir='locales', languages=[st.session_state.itaolang])
localizator.install() 
_ = localizator.gettext 

en_invol = _('''                                                                                                                                                                                
The Tao begot One.
One begot Two.
Two begot Three.
And Three begot the ten thousand things. (Tao Te Ching 道德經 42)

The freedom of choice of Tao to manifest in itself finite number of personalities was referred to as an infinite cause of emanation of the world structure. Because there is nothing unconscious, this free choice manifests first being, whose consciousness is divine plan, or idea of the development of the world structure. The word idea is used for description of being with finite consciousness which contains all possibilities of manifestation. The separated personalities are not manifested yet and exist as principles of personalities, as individualities. Consciousness of this manifested being is consciousness of all individualities. Consciousness of all individualities that contains all possibilities of free choice of all personalities is consciousness of mankind. To fulfil divine plan, mankind has the freedom of choice of all personalities.

The fulfilment of divine plan occurs in states of involution and evolution. The concept of involution signifies envelopment, folding inwards, and evolution signifies unfolding. Because everything has consciousness, involution signifies envelopment of consciousness, and evolution signifies unfolding of consciousness. Envelopment and unfolding of consciousness are connected with the freedom of choice. The free choice of Tao to become conscious in itself of manifestation of personalities, leads to manifestation of the world structure. Manifestation of consciousness of separated personalities corresponds to involution, because infinite consciousness of Tao is folding into finite consciousness of personalities through free choice of mankind. Free choice of separated personalities in the world structure corresponds to evolution because finite consciousness of personalities is unfolding into infinite consciousness of Tao. Involution and evolution of consciousness are inseparable from the freedom of choice.

So that all personalities are to be manifested equally free, they must themselves determine which consciousness every separately manifested personality will have in order to make its first free choice. This can do only all personalities together, as whole mankind, as one being. If mankind not by itself choose with what consciousness every separated personality will start to make its free choice, then the choice of all personalities, as of whole mankind would be not free and predetermined by Tao from the beginning. Then the first choice of every separately manifested personality would be not free also, what would contradict to the freedom of choice of personality. Therefore, the free choice of Tao to become conscious in itself of manifestation of finite number of personalities manifests mankind, as one being with the freedom of choice of all personalities. This free choice of Tao is called great sacrifice because now only mankind can make free choice through Tao.

The trinity

All conceptions which deserve of attention and which make an attempt to explain manifestation of the world structure refer to necessity of trinity. Therefore, all such conceptions can be characterized by one general statement, expressing the main idea of the emanation of the world structure:

One manifests Two; Two manifest Three; Three manifest the world structure.

The emanation of the world structure from and in Tao is possible because an object which Tao is conscious of in itself has consciousness and becomes subject of consciousness. Herein it is included possibility that manifested One becomes Two. However, One must be manifested first before Two can be manifested. Manifested One is not Tao because Tao is infinite, and something manifested can be only a being with finite consciousness. Manifested One can contain only one manifested world structure and only finite number of personalities in its finite consciousness. Infinite consciousness of Tao contains all countless possibilities of manifestation of the world structures and personalities.

Manifestation of One, as being with finite consciousness, begins with free choice of Tao to become conscious in itself of finite number of personalities. The result of such consciousness is manifestation which itself has consciousness and which is called mankind. This is manifested One. 

To manifest something it is possible only through the free choice. In order to make free choice, it is necessary to have the freedom of choice. Therefore, the freedom of choice must exist in all three elements of the trinity, so that the world structure could be manifested, in which finite number of personalities have freedom of choice. Because mankind is always first manifested being with freedom of choice of all personalities, it is possible to make the following statement:

Free mankind, which is conscious of itself as Unity is One.

Mankind has divine plan of the development of all possibilities of consciousness of personalities in itself. Which number of personalities must be manifested is predetermined through free choice of Tao in advance. All possibilities of any choice of personalities are also predetermined through individualities in advance. However, which relations of consciousness will be manifested between personalities, which consciousness will have every separately manifested personality, all personalities must determine together, as one whole mankind.

Manifestation of separated personalities can occur only together with manifestation of hierarchies of consciousness without freedom of choice. So that equally free personalities and hierarchies of consciousness without freedom of choice, as all possibilities of free choice of personalities, have to be manifested, it is necessary that whole mankind is conscious of duality in itself. One element of duality must correspond to all personalities with freedom of choice, and another element of duality must correspond to all hierarchies of consciousness without freedom of choice. Possibility for mankind to become conscious in itself of duality exists, as consequence of self-consciousness. Mankind cannot be not conscious of duality in itself because it has self-consciousness, mankind, however, has freedom to choose how to be conscious of duality in itself. To become conscious in itself of duality it is necessary for manifestation of the world structure. However, mankind makes its free choice to determine which relations will be manifested between elements of duality.

The free choice of mankind as One allows to become conscious of such possibilities of manifestation of all relations between two elements of duality which are most suitable for manifestation of separated free personalities. Such free choice is made from knowledge of all possibilities of free choice of all personalities. The free choice of mankind as One, allows mankind to become conscious of itself as Two. Personalities and hierarchies of consciousness exist in consciousness of mankind as two original principles. Hence, the following statement:

Free mankind, which is conscious of itself as Duality is Two.

To become conscious in itself of duality it is not enough for manifestation of plenty of  beings in the world structure yet. For this purpose it is necessary that mankind becomes conscious of trinity in itself. The possibility to become conscious of the trinity in itself exists because mankind does not lose consciousness of itself as One. Mankind is conscious of itself as One and as Two together. To be conscious of itself as One and as Two together means to become conscious of itself as Three. Mankind makes free choice of which relations of consciousness will be manifested between the elements of trinity. Therefore, it is possible to make one more statement:

Free mankind, which is conscious of itself as Trinity is Three.

Involution of consciousnesses of mankind occurs through free choice of mankind as one being, consisting of all individualities. All individualities are potentially equal and contain all possibilities of free choice of all personalities. Involution of consciousness consists of that, that mankind becomes conscious in itself of principles or ideas that can be manifested in evolution beside each other and in each other. The purpose is manifestation of separated personalities with freedom of choice and of hierarchies of consciousness without freedom of choice. 

Mankind becomes conscious of itself as One, Two and Three together. The state of consciousness as One is attained together with state of consciousness as Two and together with state of consciousness as Three.  Therefore all states of consciousness exist always together, in each other and beside each other. This means Three are One. 

There are no contradictions between spiritual science and ancient scriptures. Ancient writings, however, do not refer to the freedom of choice directly. The reason for it is that waking consciousness of man was not developed so far yet, that it was possible to speak about freedom of choice directly. Therefore ancient scriptures mention the freedom of choice indirectly. Consciousness of man, however, has changed. Responsibility of personality for its free choice changes accordingly to its consciousness. To point out to the freedom of choice became necessary because further destiny of mankind on the Earth depends on that, that every single personality will become conscious of consequences of its free choice.

The mutual existence of three states of consciousness of mankind as One, Two and Three leads to further involution of principles of consciousness, life and form. From any three elements (a, b, c), without consideration of their order, it is possible to form only seven different combinations (a, b, c, ab, bc, ac, abc). Therefore, consciousness by which mankind becomes conscious of trinity determines sevenness of consciousness. Mankind becomes conscious of trinity in itself and through trinity becomes conscious of itself, what creates seven combinations of consciousness. Free choice of mankind determines which relations of consciousness will be manifested between all possible combinations of consciousness of trinity. The result of free choice of mankind is seven combinations of consciousness of trinity, or seven principles. 

The world structure will be manifested when plenty of hierarchies of consciousness will be manifested. This occurs whilst mankind becomes conscious of plenty of principles in itself. Mankind becomes conscious of itself as One, Two, Three and so on. Further involution of consciousness occurs whilst mankind becomes conscious of sevenness, or of seven creative spirits before the throne of God. 

Before seven spirits of God can be manifested during evolution, they all must become conscious to mankind as principles during involution. Because single personalities are not manifested yet, involution of consciousness of mankind occurs through free choice of whole mankind, and not through free choice of single personalities. The result of such mutual free choice of mankind, are principles of consciousness, life and form. Mankind becomes conscious of principles in itself which can be manifested as beings with self-consciousness. Beside principles with lower consciousness mankind becomes conscious of principles with higher consciousness in itself. In such a way, involution of consciousness of mankind is involution of principles. 

Consciousness of modern man in physical body allows him to make distinction between space and time. Awareness of space is connected with manifestation of different relations between hierarchies of consciousness beside each other and in each other. Successive repetition of changes of relations between hierarchies of consciousness following one after another, leads to awareness of time. Personalities can become conscious of space and time only together with manifestation of hierarchies of consciousness. In this sense involution of consciousness of mankind is also process of wrapping up of infinite consciousness of Tao into space and time. In state of involution personalities and hierarchies of consciousness have no independent existence yet because they are only parts of consciousness of mankind. Therefore, the state of involution of consciousness of mankind is timeless and spaceless. Time and space will be manifested only in the state of evolution and exist beside each other and in each other. 

The purpose of involution of consciousness of mankind is manifestation of single personalities which are able to make their free choice. Evolution of consciousness of personalities begins with manifestation of single personalities. Because involution and evolution of consciousness are inseparable from the freedom of choice, they cannot exist without each other also. The free choice of mankind in state of involution leads to free choice of personalities in state of evolution. The change of two states of consciousness, such as for example, involution and evolution is rhythm, or cycle of consciousness.

The rhythms

In any rhythm or cycle there are always two alternating states as result of principle of duality. These two states can be considered as two opposites. Because there is nothing unconscious, rhythm can be defined as alternation or change of two states of consciousness. Such events as day and night, in-breathing and out-breathing, yin and yang and so on, are rhythms of consciousness also.

Esoteric philosophy of all times describes life of the world structure, as rhythmic life. Indian philosophy, for example, speaks of inhalation and exhalation of One. The One experiences different states of its divine life. These states are compared to in-breathing and out-breathing. Out-breathing of the One corresponds to manifestation of the world structure from Tao and in-breathing corresponds to state of dissolution of the world structure in Tao. Thus alternate the manifested and not manifested world structure, states of activity and rest. Manvantara is state of activity and Pralaya is the state of the One, resting in himself.

Basic or main rhythm of the world structure is determined by two states of consciousness, by the state of consciousness where Tao is conscious in itself of personalities, as beings with freedom of choice, and by state of consciousness where all personalities are conscious of themselves as Tao. This corresponds to manifestation of the world structure from Tao and to dissolution of the world structure in Tao. It is necessary to emphasize again that manifestation of any rhythm is result of free choice. The main rhythm is result of free choice of Tao to be conscious of finite number of personalities in itself as well as result of the free choice of all personalities to become conscious of themselves as Tao.

The numerical characteristic of this rhythm is finite number of personalities in the manifested world structure. Because manifestation of finite number of separated personalities occurs only after completion of involution of consciousness of mankind, all rhythms that could be manifested in the world structure must become conscious to mankind in state of involution. Because in the world structure must be manifested personalities with the freedom of choice and hierarchies of consciousness without freedom of choice, all rhythms must be manifested through hierarchies of consciousness without freedom of choice. In state of involution mankind becomes conscious of different rhythms of consciousness, life and form which all separated personalities must experience during involution in order to become conscious of themselves as Tao.

The state of involution of consciousness of mankind is timeless and spaceless. Space and time are manifested only in state of evolution. Evolution of consciousness of personalities occurs in space and time. Involution and evolution together form creative activity of the manifested world structure. According to Indian philosophy the creative cycle of activity must be replaced by creative inactivity in which manifested world structure is dissolved in Tao. Besides, it is mentioned that states of creative activity - Manvantara and inactivity - Pralaya have same duration.

In state of involution all personalities create no Karma yet, but free choice of mankind prepares conditions for free choice of separated personalities in evolution. Karma can be created by single personalities only in state of evolution. Therefore, state of involution can be compared with state of Pralaya, and state of evolution with state of Manvantara.

It is necessary to point out to certain difficulty which arises already by comparison of duration of involution and evolution. Involution occurs prior to manifestation of time and space. Evolution occurs in time and space. It is possible to compare only by units of time and space. Such units of comparison are rhythms which are manifested only in state of evolution. However in state of involution rhythms are not manifested yet, neither time nor space is manifested, therefore, it is impossible to compare duration of involution and evolution. Nevertheless it is possible to claim that all rhythms which mankind became conscious of in state of involution will become conscious to separated personalities in state of evolution. And in this sense it is possible to claim that involution and evolution have equal duration.

Still bigger difficulty arises by attempt to compare duration of state of the manifested world structure and duration of state in which the world structure is dissolved in Tao. Such state is also called Maha-Pralaya in Indian philosophy. Is it possible to compare the state of infinite loneliness and oneness of Tao in rhythms of the manifested world structure whose source is Tao? Indian philosophy, for example, specifies duration of our world structure in terrestrial years and equates their number to duration of Maha-Pralaya. 

Similar calculations could be found in the second volume of Secret Doctrine where the number equal to 311 040 000 000 000 terrestrial years is given. Although various calculations can differ from each other, their sense remains the same. All calculations express duration of the world structure in finite number of terrestrial years and equate it to the state of Maha-Pralaya when no world structure is manifested, when Tao dwells in its infinite loneliness and oneness.

If to suppose Tao dwells in its infinite loneliness and oneness exactly as much terrestrial years as the world structure can last, then it would mean Tao is subjected to some rhythm. Tao is source of any rhythm and can not be subjected to rhythm. May Tao, who is always conscious in itself of all possibilities of manifestation of all world structures, to be in need of such state whose duration could be measured by finite number of terrestrial days, before next world structure is manifested? If Tao is always conscious of all possibilities of manifestation of next world structure, then the state of Maha-Pralaya could pass over into state of involution at once. Even if certain pause existed between the end of preceding world structure and the beginning of next world structure, it would be impossible to measure it by units of the manifested world structure. Therefore, any such calculations can be only characteristics of the manifested world structure. In this sense that number of the terrestrial years is characteristics of number of rhythms which every personality must experience in order to become conscious of itself as Tao.

However between the states in which the world structure is manifested and is not manifested, there always exist relations to which it is possible to point out. On the one hand, in not manifested world structure all possible results of free choice are known to Tao, but free choice itself cannot be made by single personalities, because they are not manifested yet. On the other hand, in the manifested world structure, all possible results of any free choice are unknown to personalities, but free choice itself can be made. These two sides express relations which can be considered equal for manifested and not manifested world structure. These relations always exist because in infinite consciousness of Tao always exist possibilities of manifestation of new world structures.

The world structure comes to an end when every personality becomes conscious of itself as Tao. Only then the finite number of personalities can become known to every personality in the manifested world structure. Therefore, no being in the manifested world structure can know what the next world structure will be. There is no possibility to compare the present and next world structures because it is not known what may be manifested in next world structure. It is possible, however, to state, that next manifested world structure never repeats itself because the number of personalities is always different in any world structure. Next world structure cannot contain something that was already recognized by personalities through free choice in uncountable preceding world structures. Otherwise it would be known to Tao in advance which choice personalities will make and such choice would not be free. The true ‘I’ or Self of personality is Tao. Therefore, the ‘I’ of man was always manifested in personalities in preceding world structures and always will be manifested in personalities in following world structures. Knowledge about preceding and next world structure is beyond consciousness of single personality in the manifested world structure. 

Free choice of mankind in state of involution leads to further awareness of mankind of principles of consciousness, life and form. The state of involution is purely internal state where nothing is manifested externally yet, and everything what will be manifested is in consciousness of mankind. Neither principles, nor single personalities have independent existence yet. Principles get independent existence together with the manifestation of single personalities. Manifestation of single personalities signifies beginning of evolution. On transition from involution to evolution mostly lowest state of principles of consciousness, life and form is attained. This lowest state is always higher than any state of evolving single personalities and principles. 

'''
)

